      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Reopened due to problem discovered while spot-checking the 3.4.2 release:  The removal of the buildnumber plugin was not complete: The $</p>\n{buildNumber}\n<p> and $</p>\n{timestamp}\n<p> variables still exist in Server.properties and Client.properties, but are not replaced with any values.  Plan is to remove buildNumber entirely (and uses of it in the code), and to make sure timestamp is populated, possibly via another maven plugin.  This needs to happen on maintenance-3.4 and master.</p>",
     "created": "18/Jan/11 1:10 PM",
     "id": "11773",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10781/comment/11773",
